    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Statistical questions on the EST I focus on measures of centre and spread, interpreting data displays, and calculating basic probability.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Mean",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\bar{x}=\\dfrac{\\sum x}{n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Median",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "middle value when sorted",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Range",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "max \\( - \\) min",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Probability",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(E)=\\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the mean of \\( 4, 7, 7, 10, 12 \\). \\[ \\bar{x}=\\frac{4+7+7+10+12}{5}=\\frac{40}{5}=8. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Counting and probability</h3>The probability of event \\( A \\) AND event \\( B \\) (independent): \\( P(A\\cap B)=P(A)\\cdot P(B) \\). The probability of \\( A \\) OR \\( B \\): \\( P(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Statistics & Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Mean</strong> \\(=\\dfrac{\\sum x}{n}\\); <strong>Median</strong> = middle value when ordered; <strong>Mode</strong> = most frequent. <strong>Range</strong> \\(= \\max - \\min\\). <strong>IQR</strong> \\(= Q_3 - Q_1\\). <strong>Probability:</strong> \\(P(A) = \\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}}\\); \\(P(A \\cup B) = P(A)+P(B)-P(A \\cap B)\\). Mutually exclusive: \\(P(A \\cap B)=0\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Combined probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A bag has 4 red and 6 blue balls. Two are drawn without replacement. Find \\(P(\\text{both red})\\). <p>\\(P = \\dfrac{4}{10} \\times \\dfrac{3}{9} = \\dfrac{12}{90} = \\dfrac{2}{15}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "The ages of 7 students are: 14, 15, 15, 16, 16, 16, 18. A student is chosen at random. Find (a) the median age, (b) \\(P(\\text{age} > 15)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "(a) 4th value = <strong>16</strong>. (b) Ages &gt; 15: three 16s and one 18 = 4 students. \\(P = 4/7\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
